      "writtenOn": "2025-01-12T13:53:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I am not entirely sure of the reason either; it was committed by @Martin.\n\nI conducted a test on the little core running at 1.5GHz, and the average time consumption introduced by stack_trace_save_tsk is less than 2us. This is because it does not require a full stack walk. And the tracepoint is typically disabled.\n\nThe reason I placed the tracepoint after sched_switch is that Perfetto relies on the sequence of events; otherwise, the blocked reason will not be displayed.",
